Cull a stacking-context root with the boxes hoisted to it (Roves; Blitz #1493).

Base: crates.io blitz-paint 0.3.0-beta.4 (DioxusLabs/blitz
92b11f1bd8ab7975411328b0406a95a09445b4e7, packages/blitz-paint).
Applied in support/blitz-v8-probe/vendor/blitz-paint; see ROVES_PATCHES.md there.
Paired with patches/blitz-dom-0.3.0-beta.4/0004-positioned-paint-layer-tree-order.patch.

render_element culled a node when its own overflow and border box missed the clip
rectangle, but a stacking-context root also paints the boxes hoisted to it, which its
overflow need not contain; Node::hit_inner already tests them inside
StackingContext::hoisted_content_bbox. The cull extent now includes that box, so paint
and hit testing agree on which hoisted boxes exist.

diff --git a/src/render.rs b/src/render.rs
index 407fd1a..5478501 100644
--- a/src/render.rs
+++ b/src/render.rs
@@ -388,7 +388,23 @@ impl<'dom, 'a> BlitzDomPainter<'dom, 'a> {
             x: -self.initial_x,
             y: -self.initial_y,
         }) * transform;
-        let screen_bbox = screen_transform.transform_rect_bbox(overflow.union(border_box));
+        // Roves patch (Blitz #1493): a stacking-context root also paints the
+        // boxes hoisted to it, which its own overflow need not contain. Hit
+        // testing descends into them within `hoisted_content_bbox` (CSS px from
+        // the border box, like `overflow` in device px), so culling uses it too.
+        let mut paint_extent = overflow.union(border_box);
+        if let Some(sc) = node.stacking_context.as_deref()
+            && !sc.children.is_empty()
+        {
+            let hoisted = sc.hoisted_content_bbox(node.tree(), node.id, self.scale);
+            paint_extent = paint_extent.union(Rect::new(
+                hoisted.left as f64 * self.scale,
+                hoisted.top as f64 * self.scale,
+                hoisted.right as f64 * self.scale,
+                hoisted.bottom as f64 * self.scale,
+            ));
+        }
+        let screen_bbox = screen_transform.transform_rect_bbox(paint_extent);
 
         // Cull elements that fall entirely outside the current clip rectangle. In addition to
         // the viewport, `clip_rect` is narrowed by any ancestor scrollport (see below), so this
